# Public Profile SEO

Public `/estafadores/:id` and `/empresas/:id` pages must remain crawlable without relying only
on an empty SPA shell.

- Keep a unique title, description, canonical URL, Open Graph metadata, and JSON-LD per profile.
- Use `index,follow` only for active public profiles. Missing, inactive, removed, or error
  profiles must use `noindex,follow`.
- Structured data must match visible content. Use `ProfilePage` with `Person` or `Organization`;
  do not encode unverified criminal allegations as structured facts.
- Keep profile name, report count, categories, and dates accurate and escaped in generated HTML.
- Preserve build-time prerendering through `SEO_PROFILE_FEED_URL`, `VITE_SITE_URL`, and an
  absolute `VITE_API_BASE_URL`.
- Keep `sitemap.xml` limited to public indexable profiles and include `lastmod` when available.
- Keep `/reportar` and `/api/` disallowed in `robots.txt`.
- Serve identical substantive content to users and crawlers; never add bot-only rendering.
- Production hosting must serve generated profile files before SPA fallback and return real
  `404`/`410` responses for unknown or removed profiles.

When changing profile data or routing, update unit and Playwright SEO assertions.
